"""Participations in proficiency testing schemes and other interlaboratory comparisons, their
results, and the database guards that keep them.

A participation is never deleted. While it is open its fields can change, but not its method or
who planned it. Once reviewed with corrective follow-up, only the follow-up fields change, and
the closure that signs them; a closed or cancelled participation never changes. A result is
added or removed only while its participation is open and is never updated; the guard locks the
participation row it reads, as the services do. Creating the tables touches no existing record.
"""

